{"reference":"Genesis 10","book":"Genesis","chapter":10,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The movement of Genesis","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Genesis moves from universal origins in chapters 1–11 to ancestral family narratives in chapters 12–50, ending with Jacob's household in Egypt. Genesis 10 therefore stands within the transition from the account of humanity's beginnings to the family story that follows.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_010_fddf22d633dc6233fb7a6f27"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
